# Helpful Slurm debug commands (replace <JOB_ID>)
# dependency + state check (dep_debug): scontrol show job <JOB_ID> && sacct -j <JOB_ID> --format=JobID,State,ExitCode -n
# queue status:
#   squeue -j <JOB_ID>
# memory high-water mark (to confirm an OOM kill):
#   sacct -j <JOB_ID> --format=JobID,State,ExitCode,MaxRSS,ReqMem -n
#
# The 'status' column is the SUBMISSION result (SUBMITTED = the scheduler
# accepted the job), NOT the computational outcome. Authoritative per-run
# outcomes are appended below by the postprocess stage under
# '# --- ORCA outcomes ... ---' / '# --- CORVUS outcomes ... ---', and are
# detailed in orca-convergence-report.log and corvus-failed-ids.txt.

